.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH PDP8 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdp8 \- plain SIMH PDP-8 simulator console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdp8
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdp8
is the PiDP-8/I build of the SIMH PDP-8 simulator with the front-panel
code inactive: it is the same executable as
.BR pidp8i-sim (1),
started under a name that disables the panel emulation. Lamps and
switches play no part; you get the classic SIMH
.B sim>
prompt on the terminal, and
.B q
exits.
.PP
It is the engine that
.BR os8-run (1)
and the boot scripts drive non-interactively, and the way to run
PDP-8 or OS/8 images on a machine with no PiDP-8/I hardware.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/share/pidp8i/boot/
boot scripts (also the working directory of many OS/8 tools)
.TP
.B /var/lib/pidp8i/media/
the OS/8 RK05 and TU56 images
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pidp8i-sim (1),
.BR os8-run (1),
the upstream README under
.IR /usr/share/doc/pidp8i/
